.TH CHTTPSVR_DECLARE_SCOPED 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_declare_scoped \- declare a chttpsvr variable with automatic destruction
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

chttpsvr_declare_scoped(name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This macro works like chttpsvr_declare, but it also attaches a GCC
cleanup attribute.  The compiler therefore destroys the server
automatically when name leaves the scope.  It destroys the server in
exactly the way that chttpsvr_destroy does.  The macro initializes the
variable to CHTTPSVR_INVALID.  The cleanup destroys nothing when name
still holds that value at the end of the scope.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_construct_scoped (3),
.BR chttpsvr_declare (3)
